                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17709254" author="JIRAUSER298472" created="Thu, 6 Apr 2023 07:35:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Root Cause&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The model of the SQL hit is the partition column format as follows &lt;em&gt;yyyy-MM-dd&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13057103/13057103_image-2023-04-06-15-35-35-934.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;br/&gt;
The data type of the F_LOSS.SYSTEM_RUN_DATE field in the hive table is TimeStamp&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13057102/13057102_image-2023-04-06-15-36-18-911.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Convert the start/end range of the first Segment of the model into the format string of the model time partition column _ 1657497600000 -&amp;gt; &quot;2022-07-11&quot;_&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13057101/13057101_image-2023-04-06-15-39-54-901.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And in transformValue2RexLiteral method&#65292;change input to  RexLiteral &lt;br/&gt;
Since the type of the partition column field is TimeStamp, it will enter the corresponding branch.&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13057100/13057100_image-2023-04-06-15-41-10-625.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In new TimestampString(value) ,  regular matching fails, report error .&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13057099/13057099_image-2023-04-06-15-42-14-808.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The data type of the time partition column used by the model in the source table is Timestamp type.&lt;br/&gt;
The format of the model time partition column needs to be set to the following two formats, otherwise an error will be reported when entering this method.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="17709266" author="JIRAUSER298472" created="Thu, 6 Apr 2023 07:45:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fix Design&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Add check before segment range is converted to RexLiteral.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If it is a DATE or TIMESTAMP type, the segment range is converted to the corresponding partition column format.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the converted format does not match the type, the segment range will be converted twice (other types and formats remain as they are), and the format conversion rules are as follows&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;date type -&amp;gt; yyyy-MM-dd&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;timestamp type -&amp;gt; yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="17715384" author="jira-bot" created="Sun, 23 Apr 2023 06:00:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Commit 08dc9f9b35c314e5a97f4b23b3e383d12417e2bb in kylin&apos;s branch refs/heads/kylin5 from Jiale He&lt;br/&gt;
